The expanded/new THE640 coverage is present in the native run: flat distinct-key directions, tree root/sibling directions, tree elided-root/cycle handling, the expanded ancestry filter in both Name/PID directions, and the actual monitor overlay direction/heading/identity test. The tie regression is also included, covering stable PID ordering in flat and tree views over reordered inputs. The actual overlay test checks c/m/n/p key selection, both arrow directions, rank changes, and `(pid,start_time,label)` confirmation retention. These tests use in-memory monitor fixtures; they do not sample live processes or dispatch an OS signal.

## Limits and disposition

This is a focused 14-selector native run, not a full workspace or full monitor suite. The pure tests do not prove live OS PID-reuse timing, and the identity fixtures do not dispatch signals. The receipt also does not cover THE639 or THE603 counterfactual mutant kills. Those are boundaries of this evidence, rather than blockers to accepting this positive THE640 receipt.

